  "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/DataDog/datadog-lambda-js/tarball/v12.144.0",
  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/DataDog/datadog-lambda-js/zipball/v12.144.0",
  "body": "> [!IMPORTANT]\r\n> Node 18/20 layers bundle [`dd-trace` 5.135.0](https://github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-js/releases/tag/v5.135.0).\r\n> Node 22/24/26 layers bundle [`dd-trace` 6.24.0](https://github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-js/releases/tag/v6.24.0).\r\n\r\n> [!NOTE]\r\n> GovCloud publication is pending. Commercial layer publication excludes `me-south-1`.\r\n\r\n## What's Changed\r\n* feat: extract trace context from MSK events by @jcstorms1 in https://github.com/DataDog/datadog-lambda-js/pull/838\r\n* test: deprecate aws lambda based integration tests because now we have e2e and the RIE based tests by @joeyzhao2018 in https://github.com/DataDog/datadog-lambda-js/pull/826\r\n* feat(appsec): publish response body on end invocation by @CarlesDD in https://github.com/DataDog/datadog-lambda-js/pull/825\r\n* test(integration): add timeout golden coverage by @joeyzhao2018 in https://github.com/DataDog/datadog-lambda-js/pull/842\r\n* fix(deps): vuln minor: sprintf-js · patch: brace-expansion [package.json] by @gh-worker-campaigns-3e9aa4[bot] in https://github.com/DataDog/datadog-lambda-js/pull/848\r\n* Bump build layer expiry to 1 day by @rithikanarayan in https://github.com/DataDog/datadog-lambda-js/pull/852\r\n* docs(integration): assign each Lambda case to one validation level by @joeyzhao2018 in https://github.com/DataDog/datadog-lambda-js/pull/851\r\n* chore: update CODEOWNERS by @joeyzhao2018 in https://github.com/DataDog/datadog-lambda-js/pull/853\r\n* skip publishing in me south 1 by @ojproductions in https://github.com/DataDog/datadog-lambda-js/pull/856\r\n* fix(trace): keep sampling priority numeric in SpanContextWrapper.fromTraceContext by @SiddhithaBhoopathy in https://github.com/DataDog/datadog-lambda-js/pull/850\r\n* fix(layer): ship the native addon versions dd-trace declares by @joeyzhao2018 in https://github.com/DataDog/datadog-lambda-js/pull/857\r\n* fix(deps): bump dd-trace to 6.24.0 and 5.135.0 for CVE-2026-116693 by @pablomartinezbernardo in https://github.com/DataDog/datadog-lambda-js/pull/860\r\n* v12.144.0 by @pablomartinezbernardo in https://github.com/DataDog/datadog-lambda-js/pull/864\r\n\r\n## New Contributors\r\n* @SiddhithaBhoopathy made their first contribution in https://github.com/DataDog/datadog-lambda-js/pull/850\r\n\r\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/DataDog/datadog-lambda-js/compare/v12.143.0...v12.144.0\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\nThe release candidate ran in Node 24 development self-monitoring for 15 hours, from November 10 at 18:20 CET to November 11 at 09:20 CET. [Candidate E2E passed](https://gitlab.ddbuild.io/DataDog/serverless-e2e-tests/-/pipelines/152161845); known LLMObs usage-metric expected failures remain tracked separately.\r\n\r\n## Layer ARNs\r\n```\r\narn:aws:lambda:<AWS_REGION>:464622532012:layer:Datadog-Node18-x:144\r\narn:aws:lambda:<AWS_REGION>:464622532012:layer:Datadog-Node20-x:144\r\narn:aws:lambda:<AWS_REGION>:464622532012:layer:Datadog-Node22-x:144\r\narn:aws:lambda:<AWS_REGION>:464622532012:layer:Datadog-Node24-x:144\r\narn:aws:lambda:<AWS_REGION>:464622532012:layer:Datadog-Node26-x:144\r\n\r\narn:aws-us-gov:lambda:us-gov-<AWS_REGION>:002406178527:layer:Datadog-Node18-x:144\r\narn:aws-us-gov:lambda:us-gov-<AWS_REGION>:002406178527:layer:Datadog-Node20-x:144\r\narn:aws-us-gov:lambda:us-gov-<AWS_REGION>:002406178527:layer:Datadog-Node22-x:144\r\narn:aws-us-gov:lambda:us-gov-<AWS_REGION>:002406178527:layer:Datadog-Node24-x:144\r\narn:aws-us-gov:lambda:us-gov-<AWS_REGION>:002406178527:layer:Datadog-Node26-x:144\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe ARNs above use `us-east-1`; substitute the AWS region where you deploy.\r\n",
  "mentions_count": 7
}
